From 6e4bf80087438192cbfb0a03d382e60db44e355c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:24:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Dispatch mode on for blasts, and it reaches the drivers
 without a dispatcher

Three corrections on top of #207, which merged an earlier draft of the same
work.

1. "Text dispatch where applicable" now defaults ON for the Text a Group
   modal, and stays OFF for the board's "text selected loads" -- the second is
   a message about a load someone is already running, not a solicitation. Each
   opener sets it; the markup carries no `checked` attribute, because the two
   openers disagree on purpose and a markup default could only be wrong for
   one of them.

2. A member with no dispatcher number falls back to their own cell again
   rather than being skipped. #207 skipped them, which reads as the safer
   choice until the numbers are counted: a THIRD of every pool has no
   dispatcher number on file -- 204 of 538 preferred, 999 of 3,128 Atlanta,
   107 of 202 Mondelez. With dispatch mode now on by default, skipping would
   have quietly cut a third of the drivers out of every blast. Reaching them
   matters more than the channel.

   The fallback is flagged rather than hidden: applyPhoneMode() sets
   directPhoneFallback and the progress panel names those drivers, because
   this message is about to land on their personal phone and they are exactly
   the list worth filling dispatcher numbers in for. The silence was the bug,
   not the fallback.

3. The Do not text checkbox moves above Driver cell and loses its
   explanation -- just the box and the label.

scripts/do-not-text-driver.test.mjs is updated to match and verified red
against the default reverting to off and against the fallback being removed
again. scripts/text-modal-layout.test.mjs pins the fourth note folding into
the same Details summary rather than being emitted loose.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
